List the entries in a tablet folder ("/" by default) on standard output.
Names follow the device tree exactly, including NOTE/Note and
DOCUMENT/Document. --ids adds the identifiers. No file is downloaded or
changed.
FLAGS shows R for recognized handwriting and H for a sibling .mark.
Documents fold their full-name .mark sidecars; --marks keeps raw sidecars
visible. --recognition reads unknown .note bodies through the cache, with
progress; --offline uses cached bodies only.

Usage:
  snctl ls [path] [flags]

Examples:
snctl ls DOCUMENT/Document
snctl ls NOTE/Note --ids --json

Flags:
  -h, --help[=true|false]          help for ls
      --ids[=true|false]           show entry identifiers
      --marks[=true|false]         show raw .mark files as separate entries
      --recognition[=true|false]   read unknown .note bodies to discover recognized handwriting

Global Flags:
      --color string            color a table: auto, always or never (default "auto")
      --format string           answer format: table, plain or json (or SNCTL_FORMAT; default: table on a terminal, plain otherwise)
      --json[=true|false]       print answers as JSON (the same as --format json)
      --no-cache[=true|false]   neither read nor write the cache on disk
      --offline[=true|false]    read cached listings and bodies without any request
  -P, --profile string          account profile (or SNCTL_PROFILE)
      --quiet[=true|false]      hide progress lines
  -v, --verbose[=true|false]    log what happens on standard error
  -y, --yes[=true|false]        confirm a command that changes settings or cloud data
